{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Protect the 2027 ILR eligibility of existing UK visa holders",
        "additional_details": "Those due to qualify for ILR in 2027 have little time to adapt. Many have completed tests and application preparations. Employers have planned sponsorship, CoS arrangements and 2027 budgets around their expected settlement dates, without allocating funds for further visa extensions. Sudden changes could leave workers without sponsorship, facing unexpected costs or job loss. Unlike those with years to adjust, this group needs a one-off transition to honour commitments made under existing rules.",
        "background": "Introduce a one-off transitional arrangement allowing existing visa holders who would qualify for Indefinite Leave to Remain (ILR) by 31 December 2027 under the rules in place before the Earned Settlement reforms to apply under those rules.",
